From: Martin Jungblut Schreiner <martin.schreiner@suse.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Build the bundled fontconfig with Python 3.6

fontconfig 2.18.3 generates fcgenericfamily.gperf with fc-genericfamily.py,
which calls sys.stdout.reconfigure() whenever stdout is not UTF-8 (the C
locale of a package build). reconfigure() only exists since Python 3.7; SLE
15 has 3.6, so the bundled fontconfig fails with

  AttributeError: '_io.TextIOWrapper' object has no attribute 'reconfigure'

The build passes -o and the script opens that file as UTF-8 itself, so the
call can simply be skipped where it is unavailable.

--- a/external/fontconfig/UnpackedTarball_fontconfig.mk
+++ b/external/fontconfig/UnpackedTarball_fontconfig.mk
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 	external/fontconfig/fontconfig-2.12.1.patch.1 \
 	external/fontconfig/nowarnnoconfig.patch.1 \
 	external/fontconfig/apple-xlocale.patch.1 \
+	external/fontconfig/python36-no-reconfigure.patch.1 \
 ))
 
 ifneq ($(OS),MACOSX)
--- a/external/fontconfig/python36-no-reconfigure.patch.1
+++ b/external/fontconfig/python36-no-reconfigure.patch.1
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+fc-genericfamily.py: do not call sys.stdout.reconfigure() where it does not
+exist. It needs Python >= 3.7, and SLE 15 builds with Python 3.6.
+
+--- a/fc-genericfamily/fc-genericfamily.py
++++ b/fc-genericfamily/fc-genericfamily.py
+@@ -142,8 +142,9 @@
+ 
+ 
+ def main():
+-    # Ensure stdout uses UTF-8 encoding
+-    if sys.stdout.encoding != 'utf-8':
++    # Ensure stdout uses UTF-8 encoding (reconfigure() needs Python >= 3.7;
++    # only matters for "-o -", files are opened as UTF-8 below)
++    if sys.stdout.encoding != 'utf-8' and hasattr(sys.stdout, 'reconfigure'):
+         sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8')
+ 
+     parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
